.TH HTTP_SOCKET 3
.SH NAME
http_socket \- create the socket of an HTTP client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int http_socket(http* " h ", int " nonblock ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_socket ()
creates a TCP socket for
.IR h ,
for https also the TLS client (the host name is announced with
.BR tls_servername (3),
so servers that host many names pick the right certificate), registers the socket with io(3), switches it to non-blocking mode if
.I nonblock
is not 0 and sets up the input buffer (16 kilobytes) and the output buffer (32 kilobytes) with
.BR http_socket_read (3)
and
.BR http_socket_write (3)
as their operations. Buffers that are there already are kept.
.P
It is called by
.BR http_open (3);
only a caller that connects the socket by itself needs it.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The descriptor, -1 on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_open(3), http_socket_read(3), http_socket_write(3)
